Apple's Game Porting Toolkit and D3DMetal are never part of G-Player and are never downloaded by it.
G-Player can use a copy the user installed or downloaded from Apple themselves, only when they turn it on in Settings;
it then copies D3DMetal, checking that D3DMetal.framework and libd3dshared.dylib are signed by Apple, into the user's library and their G-Player Wine engine.

